  "notes": "Boot a Doctor Who ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, wait out the power-up mechanism test, open the service menu, start T.1 SWITCH EDGES, then drive each public level of the ordinary switches 41, 78, 57, 47, 82, 68, 88 and 38, the Fliptronic lower-flipper buttons 112 and 114, and the ten optos PinMAME's dwGameData mask inverts (31-33 and 71-77) separately, holding each level for 2 s. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings a name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active.",
